Description: A standalone native R/C++ port of the Python 'graph-tool' network
    analysis library (<https://graph-tool.skewed.de/>), derived from 'graph-tool'
    release 3.9 without any Python runtime dependency. Incorporates 'graph-tool's
    C++ adjacency structure and provides multi-threaded native C++ implementations
    of Bayesian stochastic block model (SBM) inference (flat, nested, overlapping,
    weighted, layered, planted-partition, ordered/ranked, and bipartite SBMs),
    merge-split MCMC posterior sampling, partition mode clustering, Bayesian
    model selection, uncertain network and triadic-closure reconstruction,
    network reconstruction from Ising, epidemic, Gaussian, and Potts dynamics,
    centrality, shortest-path, connectivity, clustering, and random-graph
    algorithms, native '.gt' binary I/O and 'igraph' conversion, SFDP
    force-directed layouts, interactive HTML5 animations, vector/raster plotting
    and offline geographic map projections, and a public C++ extension header
    interface.
URL: https://github.com/diogro/rgraphtool, https://diogro.github.io/rgraphtool/
